-- ccc13-index.l4 -- the punishments and the class of the offence, by Provision of the Code (section and subsection), for the offences of Parts X and XI in this part's range.
-- GENERATED by work/gen_index.py from the per-offence functions of the other ccc13 modules: each arm calls one of them and states nothing of its own.
-- It answers the seams other parts ask of the offence sections (sentencing, attempts and parties, interim release, the list of offences triable by a provincial court judge):
--   the punishment the offence charged is liable to, and its class. A provision that is not an offence of this range, or whose penalty turns on a fact
--   (s 380(1): the value; s 430(4.11): the number of the offence; s 445.01(2): whether a law enforcement animal was killed), answers NOTHING here.
-- The section 787(1) answer is an input, because the text says "punishable on summary conviction" and states no penalty there.
-- Sections 407 to 411 have their penalty in section 412(1): the arms for them call `s 412(1) the punishments`.

§ `Parts X and XI -- the penalty of an offence, by the provision that creates it`

